= Field methods

== Measuring the canopy

1. Mark the plot centre and record the slope direction.
2. Estimate canopy cover from four directions and keep the median value.
3. Photograph the canopy from the same position on each visit.
4. Note any gap that opens after weather damage or pruning.

The canopy estimate is a field observation, not a replacement for a densiometer.
Use the same observer and the same reference chart across a season when
possible.

== Review checklist

- Confirm that every canopy value names its plot.
- Keep the light rating separate from the canopy percentage.
- Check that a repeated canopy photograph uses the same exposure.
- Remove duplicate measurements before summarizing the notebook.

